png", "id": "423398472215020", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/38974891_423398475548353_5249155989052516159_n.png?_nc_cat=109&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=zhcC5EFc9M4Q7kNvwFKR8Xs&_nc_oc=AdqG-pbPY0ywejCTWc-WiB1QKM3x6F5rgEpyU3QMvvQb_Fb2PyoZkoAfdK1uKyWope8&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQTISasdnyUgnEQbcuynBos92MRdZbKmbospAp86EEqxAQ&oe=6B0DBE46"}, "display_name": "Touchy Feely", "keywords": [], "long_description": "This is the first draft of a system I want to use to build experiences with hand tracking, it features\n\n - touch response, this is colour and sound for temperature and pressure\n - custom shader, I'm learning shader graph and want to make a battered comic book style\n\nWhat I hope to do\n\n - create a small short story in this space, about someone packing down the apartment of a loved one that has passed away.\n - polish the grab and feedback mechanics based on some feedback\n - add teleport and explore hand based teleport\n - work on more natural engaging interactions\n\nI'm making this public to get a read on the grabbing and the art style, I still want to add audio and polish the mechanics. My goal is also to create technical and creative experiments and share them. I want to publish often and develop in public! You can see all my development work at https://www.twitch.tv/samueltates and develop with me on Saturday mornings!!!", "short_description": "a hand tracking playspace, testing out grabbing and visual / audio feedback\n"}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://www.samueltate.com/", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Sam!", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://www.samueltate.com/", "category": "APPS", "comfort_rating": "NOT_RATED", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1819021644882647"}, {"id": "514087707868